      "content": "1. Understanding the Purpose of Fill in the Blanks"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fill in the Blanks questions assess core grammar rules including verbs, tenses, subject-verb agreement, and prepositions.",
        "Contextual clues such as logic, tone, singular/plural markers, and collocations guide accurate option selection.",
        "Double blank questions require analyzing both missing words simultaneously to ensure complete grammatical and logical coherence.",
        "Applying strategic elimination and avoiding overthinking are critical for speed and precision in competitive exams."
      ],
